 "notes": "P1 (RESEARCH_TREE D11, look 3/40 M6_factorial): M6 cell (3). Flags carried: W3-D1, W3-MEV (mevalonate core non-lethal under serum on ~all lines), W2-SHUF, W2-MOPEN. Methods: H1/H2 generic; P1[H1] = M6:H1+Bloo/M2(f=1); P1[H2] = M6:H2+Bloo/M2(f=1) (within-parent arm); M2[H1] = M6:H1/M2(f=1), the attribution arm (ii) 'medium alone' (M0 -> M2(f=1) on the generic parent H1 = G*). Curation (W5) and context (M5) not selected (\u00a710.1, A12c): (iii) and (v) 'lever not selected'; (iv) 'constraints alone' = P1 with generic GPRs vs G* = P1 itself vs G* (identical to (i) by construction). Calls: p57/pgr under the literal paper protocol (each task with its own inputs, GR = growth on Ham's) from the Essential-task matrix re-run with the B-loo biomass (scripts/t1_prep_tasks.py), hence line-constant per parent; fba = ratio_r < 0.01 of the line's M2(f=1) score (line-specific). No failed build (M6 sweeps 42/42 ok; no non-finite score). Test-line score and call files are git-ignored under results/m6/tmp/t1/ and regenerable by scripts/t1_prep_build.py. Gene annotations: 6 of 8 classes (gene_less_bypass and model_contradicted_loss not annotated). bootstrap_method from the \u00a76.5 training skew check: skew C1 0.0327, C1b 0.3883 (n = 686 training lines) -> percentile."
